9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI3Mzkt/MTQyNjIzMTk0Ny02/OTIxLmdpZg.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/pTth8xfl8UpdPsRjl7uyj0Um7wG-IPrlBKu74KiLYeo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI3Mzkt/MTQyNjIzMTk0Ny02/OTIxLmdpZg.jpeg","profile":"Actually appears as \"[b]Profile[/b]\" only. May also appear as \"Profile Records Ltd\" on some UK releases.\r\nProfile was one of the earliest hip-hop labels which also released disco, dance, and electro records. The label was founded in New York City in 1981 by [a=Steve Plotnicki] and [a=Cory Robbins].  Over the years Profile acquired many smaller record labels under their Profile Associated Labels umbrella imprint. Releases on Profile Associated usually occur in a label's later releases and catalog numbers on these releases start with PAL.\r\nPromotion for the label was handled in the 1980s by [a=Manny Bella] (urban) and [a=Claudia Cuseta] (dance).\r\nCory Robbins left the label in 1995 and founded [l=Robbins Entertainment]. Steve Plotnicki remained with the label unti he decided to sell it in 1997. After a fierce bidding war between [l=Tommy Boy Music] and [l=BMG]'s [l=Arista] Records, the latter won, and what was in print at the time was reissued with new BMG catalog numbers. Some new product was released since then, but it was eventually shut down by its new parent and its artists became Arista artists, but were eventually dropped by the label anyway. The offices that it occupied were once those of [l=Koch Records].\r\nAlso known as just Profile.\r\nFor companies, see [l=Profile Records Ltd.] (UK) or [l=Profile Records, Inc.] (US)","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:2739","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":362,"name":"Arista"},"sublabels":[{"id":40072,"name":"Another Planet Records (2)"},{"id":71799,"name":"Blue Chip Records (2)"},{"id":17414,"name":"City Street Records"},{"id":3382,"name":"Invasion Recordings"},{"id":330599,"name":"Mr. Magic's Rap Attack"},{"id":24906,"name":